ed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~run_step~~CalledByGraph proc~run_step run_step proc~evaluate_energy_gradient evaluate_energy_gradient proc~evaluate_energy_gradient->proc~run_step proc~worker_loop worker_loop proc~worker_loop->proc~run_step proc~write_final_single_point write_final_single_point proc~write_final_single_point->proc~run_step proc~probe_gradient probe_gradient proc~probe_gradient->proc~evaluate_energy_gradient proc~run_geometry_optimization run_geometry_optimization proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~worker_loop proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~write_final_single_point proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~probe_gradient program~main main program~main->proc~run_geometry_optimization Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private :: wants_output Source Code subroutine run_step ( step_config , result , write_output ) !! One calculation at the current geometry, on the frozen term list !! !! Every rank calls this, and every rank must reach it with the same !! configuration -- the four combinations of bonds and frozen terms are !! written out here once rather than at each of the three call sites, !! which is where they had already started to drift. use mqc_driver , only : run_calculation type ( driver_config_t ), intent ( in ) :: step_config type ( calculation_result_t ), intent ( out ) :: result logical , intent ( in ), optional :: write_output logical :: wants_output wants_output = . false . if ( present ( write_output )) wants_output = write_output if ( ctx_terms_frozen ) then if ( ctx_has_bonds ) then call run_calculation ( ctx_resources , step_config , ctx_sys_geom , ctx_bonds , & result , write_output = wants_output , & supplied_terms = ctx_terms , n_supplied_terms = ctx_n_terms ) else call run_calculation ( ctx_resources , step_config , ctx_sys_geom , & result_out = result , write_output = wants_output , & supplied_terms = ctx_terms , n_supplied_terms = ctx_n_terms ) end if else if ( ctx_has_bonds ) then call run_calculation ( ctx_resources , step_config , ctx_sys_geom , ctx_bonds , & result , write_output = wants_output ) else call run_calculation ( ctx_resources , step_config , ctx_sys_geom , & result_out = result , write_output = wants_output ) end if end if end subroutine run_step","tags":"","url":"proc/run_step.html"},{"title":"send_final_geometry – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine send_final_geometry(comm, sys_geom) Move a geometry to the workers, with the command already sent Separate from send_geometry only in that the caller has already\nchosen and broadcast the command – EVALUATE or FINAL. Splitting the\ntwo keeps the “one broadcast integer then the coordinates” order in\none place, which is the order worker_loop reads them in. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(comm_t), intent(in) :: comm type( system_geometry_t ), intent(in) :: sys_geom Calls proc~~send_final_geometry~~CallsGraph proc~send_final_geometry send_final_geometry bcast bcast proc~send_final_geometry->