s are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=dp), private, allocatable :: buffer (:) integer(kind=int32), private :: n Source Code subroutine send_final_geometry ( comm , sys_geom ) !! Move a geometry to the workers, with the command already sent !! !! Separate from `send_geometry` only in that the caller has already !! chosen and broadcast the command -- EVALUATE or FINAL. Splitting the !! two keeps the \"one broadcast integer then the coordinates\" order in !! one place, which is the order `worker_loop` reads them in. type ( comm_t ), intent ( in ) :: comm type ( system_geometry_t ), intent ( in ) :: sys_geom real ( dp ), allocatable :: buffer (:) integer ( int32 ) :: n ! Flat, because pic-mpi broadcasts rank-1 arrays and the coordinates are ! rank-2. reshape rather than a pointer remap: this is 3N doubles once ! per step, against an SCF, and the copy is not measurable. n = int ( 3 * sys_geom % total_atoms , int32 ) allocate ( buffer ( n )) buffer = reshape ( sys_geom % coordinates , [ 3 * sys_geom % total_atoms ]) call bcast ( comm , buffer , n , 0_int32 ) deallocate ( buffer ) end subroutine send_final_geometry","tags":"","url":"proc/send_final_geometry.html"},{"title":"send_geometry – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine send_geometry(comm, sys_geom) Rank 0’s half of an ordinary optimization step Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(comm_t), intent(in) :: comm type( system_geometry_t ), intent(in) :: sys_geom Calls proc~~send_geometry~~CallsGraph proc~send_geometry send_geometry bcast bcast proc~send_geometry->bcast proc~send_final_geometry send_final_geometry proc~send_geometry->proc~send_final_geometry proc~send_final_geometry->bcast Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Pro