es which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~add_method~~CalledByGraph proc~add_method add_method proc~calculation_fingerprint calculation_fingerprint proc~calculation_fingerprint->proc~add_method proc~run_calculation run_calculation proc~run_calculation->proc~calculation_fingerprint proc~run_fragmented_calculation run_fragmented_calculation proc~run_calculation->proc~run_fragmented_calculation proc~run_fragmented_calculation->proc~calculation_fingerprint proc~compute_energy_and_forces compute_energy_and_forces proc~compute_energy_and_forces->proc~run_calculation proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations run_multi_molecule_calculations proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations->proc~run_calculation proc~run_step run_step proc~run_step->proc~run_calculation proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~run_calculation proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~run_calculation program~main main program~main->proc~run_calculation program~main->proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations proc~evaluate_energy_gradient evaluate_energy_gradient proc~evaluate_energy_gradient->proc~run_step proc~mqc_run mqc_run proc~mqc_run->proc~session_run proc~worker_loop worker_loop proc~worker_loop->proc~run_step proc~worker_loop~2 worker_loop proc~worker_loop~2->proc~worker_run proc~write_final_single_point write_final_single_point proc~write_final_single_point->proc~run_step proc~probe_gradient probe_gradient proc~probe_gradient->proc~evaluate_energy_gradient proc~run_geometry_optimization run_geometry_optimization proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~worker_loop proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~write_final_single_point proc~session_begin mqc_session_t%session_begin proc~session_begin->proc~worker_loop~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine add_method ( h , config ) !! Everything that decides what number a fragment gets !! !! Only the branch that will actually run is hashed. A deck carrying !! stale `dft` settings while running xTB would otherwise fingerprint !! differently from the same xTB calculation written cleanly, and the two !! compute the same thing. type ( hasher_t ), intent ( inout ) :: h type ( method_config_t ), intent ( in ) :: config call h % text ( \"method\" ) call h % int ( int ( config % method_type )) select case ( config % method_type ) case ( METHOD_TYPE_GFN1 , METHOD_TYPE_GFN2 ) call h % text ( \"xtb\" ) call h % real ( config % xtb % accuracy ) call h % real ( config % xtb % electronic_temp ) call h % text ( trim ( config % xtb % solvent )) call h % text ( trim ( config % xtb % solvation_model )) call h % flag ( config % xtb % use_cds ) call h % flag ( config % xtb % use_shift ) call h % real ( config % xtb % dielectric ) call h % int ( config % xtb % cpcm_nang ) call h % real ( config % xtb % cpcm_rscale ) ! maxiter is in because it decides whether the SCF converged, and an ! energy from a run that stopped early is not the same number. call h % int ( config % scf % max_iter ) case default ! HF, DFT and anything else built on the SCF. call h % text ( trim ( config % basis_set )) call h % flag ( config % use_spherical ) call h % text ( trim ( config % scf % aux_basis_set )) call h % text ( trim ( config % scf % guess )) call h % flag ( config % scf % unrestricted ) call h % int ( config % scf % max_iter ) call h % real ( config % scf % energy_convergence ) call h % real ( config % scf % density_convergence ) if ( config % method_type == METHOD_TYPE_DFT ) then call h % text ( \"dft\" ) call h % text ( trim ( config % dft % functional )) call h % text ( trim ( config % dft % grid_type )) call h % int ( config % dft % radial_points ) call h % int ( config % dft % angular_points ) end if end select end subroutine add_method","tags":"","url":"proc/add_method.html"},{"title":"add_system – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine add_system(h, sys) Everything about the molecule and how it is cut up Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( hasher_t ), intent(inout) :: h type( system_geometry_t ), intent(in) :: sys Calls proc~~add_system~~CallsGraph proc~add_system add_system proc~hash_int_array hasher_t%hash_int_array proc~add_system->proc~hash_int_array proc~hash_real_array hasher_t%hash_real_array proc~add_system->proc~hash_real_array proc~hash_text hasher_t%hash_text proc~add_system->proc~hash_text proc~hash_byte hasher_t%hash_byte proc~hash_text->proc~hash_byte Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~add_system~~CalledByGraph proc~add_system add_system proc~calculation_fingerprint calculation_fingerprint proc~calculation_fingerprint->proc~add_system proc~run_calculation run_calculation proc~run_calculation->proc~calculation_fingerprint proc~run_fragmented_calculation run_fragmented_calculation proc~run_calculation->proc~run_fragmented_calculation proc~run_fragmented_calculation->proc~calculation_fingerprint proc~compute_energy_and_forces compute_energy_and_forces proc~compute_energy_and_forces->proc~run_calculation proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations run_multi_molecule_calculations proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations->proc~run_calculation proc~run_step run_step proc~run_step->proc~run_calculation proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~run_calculation proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~run_calculation program~main main program~main->proc~run_calculation program~main->proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations proc~evaluate_energy_gradient evaluate_energy_gradient proc~evaluate_energy_gradient->proc~run_step proc~mqc_run mqc_run proc~mqc_run->proc~session_run proc~worker_loop worker_loop proc~worker_loop->proc~run_step proc~worker_loop~2 worker_loop proc~worker_loop~2->proc~worker_run proc~write_final_single_point write_final_single_point proc~write_final_single_point->proc~run_step proc~probe_gradient probe_gradient proc~probe_gradient->proc~evaluate_energy_gradient proc~run_geometry_optimization run_geometry_optimization proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~worker_loop proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~write_final_single_point proc~session_begin mqc_session_t%session_begin proc~session_begin->proc~worker_loop~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: imon integer, private :: islot Source Code subroutine add_system ( h , sys ) !! Everything about the molecule and how it is cut up type ( hasher_t ), intent ( inout ) :: h type ( system_geometry_t ), intent ( in ) :: sys integer :: imon , islot call h % text ( \"system\" ) call h % int ( sys % total_atoms ) call h % int ( sys % charge ) call h % int ( sys % multiplicity ) if ( allocated ( sys % element_numbers )) call h % int_array ( sys % element_numbers ) if ( allocated ( sys % coordinates )) call h % real_array ( reshape ( sys % coordinates , & [ size ( sys % coordinates )])) ! The partition. A term list names monomers by index, so two runs that ! agree on the atoms and disagree on the grouping agree on nothing that ! matters -- term (1,2) is a different dimer in each. call h % text ( \"monomers\" ) call h % int ( sys % n_monomers ) if ( allocated ( sys % fragment_sizes )) then call h % int_array ( sys % fragment_sizes ) do imon = 1 , sys % n_monomers do islot = 1 , sys % fragment_sizes ( imon ) call h % int ( sys % fragment_atoms ( islot , imon )) end do end do end if if ( allocated ( sys % fragment_charges )) call h % int_array ( sys % fragment_charges ) if ( allocated ( sys % fragment_multiplicities )) then call h % int_array ( sys % fragment_multiplicities ) end if ! Bonds decide where caps go, and a cap is an atom that was not there ! before. `is_broken` is derived from the partition, so it is not hashed ! separately -- the partition above already covers it. call h % text ( \"bonds\" ) if ( allocated ( sys % bonds )) then call h % int ( size ( sys % bonds )) do imon = 1 , size ( sys % bonds ) call h % int ( sys % bonds ( imon )% atom_i ) call h % int ( sys % bonds ( imon )% atom_j ) call h % int ( sys % bonds ( imon )% order ) end do else call h % int ( 0 ) end if end subroutine add_system","tags":"","url":"proc/add_system.html"},{"title":"hash_byte – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine hash_byte(this, value) Fold one byte in Type Bound hasher_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( hasher_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: value Called by proc~~hash_byte~~CalledByGraph proc~hash_byte hasher_t%hash_byte proc~hash_int hasher_t%hash_int proc~hash_int->proc~hash_byte proc~hash_real hasher_t%hash_real proc~hash_real->proc~hash_byte proc~hash_text hasher_t%hash_text proc~hash_text->proc~hash_byte proc~add_method add_method proc~add_method->proc~hash_text proc~add_system add_system proc~add_system->proc~hash_text proc~calculation_fingerprint calculation_fingerprint proc~calculation_fingerprint->proc~hash_text proc~calculation_fingerprint->proc~add_method proc~calculation_fingerprint->proc~add_system proc~run_calculation run_calculation proc~run_calculation->proc~calculation_fingerprint proc~run_fragmented_calculation run_fragmented_calculation proc~run_calculation->proc~run_fragmented_calculation proc~run_fragmented_calculation->proc~calculation_fingerprint proc~compute_energy_and_forces compute_energy_and_forces proc~compute_energy_and_forces->proc~run_calculation proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations run_multi_molecule_calculations proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations->proc~run_calculation proc~run_step run_step proc~run_step->proc~run_calculation proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~run_calculation proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~run_calculation program~main main program~main->proc~run_calculation program~main->proc~run_multi_molecule_calculations proc~evaluate_energy_gradient evaluate_energy_gradien