e to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=12), private :: buffer Source Code pure function integer_to_key ( value ) result ( key ) !! An integer as the string BSE keys its elements by integer , intent ( in ) :: value character ( len = :), allocatable :: key character ( len = 12 ) :: buffer write ( buffer , \"(I0)\" ) value key = trim ( buffer ) end function integer_to_key","tags":"","url":"proc/integer_to_key.html"},{"title":"build_molecular_ecp_json – metalquicha","text":"public  subroutine build_molecular_ecp_json(json_path, element_symbols, mol_ecp, error) Build a per-atom ECP set for a list of atoms Each distinct element is read once and copied to every atom of that\nelement, as the orbital basis reader does – parsing the same file per\natom would dominate the setup for anything but a tiny molecule. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: json_path character(len=*), intent(in) :: element_symbols (:) type( molecular_ecp_type ), intent(out) :: mol_ecp type( error_t ), intent(out) :: error Calls proc~~build_molecular_ecp_json~~CallsGraph proc~build_molecular_ecp_json build_molecular_ecp_json proc~atomic_ecp_destroy atomic_ecp_type%atomic_ecp_destroy proc~build_molecular_ecp_json->proc~atomic_ecp_destroy proc~copy_atomic_ecp copy_atomic_ecp proc~build_molecular_ecp_json->proc~copy_atomic_ecp proc~element_symbol_to_number element_symbol_to_number proc~build_molecular_ecp_json->proc~element_symbol_to_number proc~error_add_context error_t%error_add_context proc~build_molecular_ecp_json->proc~error_add_context proc~error_has_error error_t%error_h