onfig->module~mqc_method_types module~mqc_physical_constants->pic_types module~mqc_xyz_reader->module~mqc_error module~mqc_xyz_reader->pic_types module~mqc_xyz_reader->module~mqc_geometry module~mqc_calculation_defaults->pic_types module~mqc_method_types->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Build an effective fragment potential for the whole system and write it Only rank zero does anything: the work is one SCF and a set of response\nsolves, all of them threaded inside the integral backend, and the write is\na single file. Distributing it would mean every rank recomputing the same\npotential to overwrite the same path. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( driver_config_t ), intent(in) :: config type( system_geometry_t ), intent(in) :: sys_geom integer, intent(in) :: rank Calls proc~~run_makefp~~CallsGraph proc~run_makefp run_makefp error error proc~run_makefp->error info info proc~run_makefp->info proc~element_number_to_symbol element_number_to_symbol proc~run_makefp->proc~element_number_to_symbol proc~error_get_message error_t%error_get_message proc~run_makefp->proc~error_get_message proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~run_makefp->proc~error_has_error proc~get_basename get_basename proc~run_makefp->proc~get_basename proc~run_libcint_makefp run_libcint_makefp proc~run_makefp->proc~run_libcint_makefp proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~run_libcint_makefp->proc~error_set Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Functio