, atom_j, nfrag, fragments) result(broken) Whether fragmentation severs the bond between two atoms Broken means the two atoms do not belong to the same set of fragments.\nComparing sets rather than asking “are they both in some fragment”\nis what makes this correct for overlapping fragments, where an atom\ncan legitimately be in more than one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: atom_i integer, intent(in) :: atom_j integer, intent(in) :: nfrag type( input_fragment_t ), intent(in), allocatable :: fragments (:) Return Value logical Called by proc~~bond_is_broken~~CalledByGraph proc~bond_is_broken bond_is_broken proc~read_connectivity read_connectivity proc~read_connectivity->proc~bond_is_broken proc~read_molecule read_molecule proc~read_molecule->proc~read_connectivity proc~populate_config populate_config proc~populate_config->proc~read_molecule proc~read_json_config_file read_json_config_file proc~read_json_config_file->proc~populate_config proc~read_json_config_text read_json_config_text proc~read_json_config_text->proc~populate_config proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~read_json_config_text proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~read_json_config_text program~main main program~main->proc~read_json_config_file Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: ifrag logical, private :: in_i logical, private :: in_j Source Code pure function bond_is_broken ( atom_i , atom_j , nfrag , fragments ) result ( broken ) !! Whether fragmentation severs the bond between two atoms !! !! Broken means the two atoms do not belong to the same set of fragments. !! Comparing *sets* rather than asking \"are they both in some fragment\" !! is what makes this correct for overlapping fragments, where an atom !! can legitimately be in more than one. integer , intent ( in ) :: atom_i , atom_j integer , intent ( in ) :: nfrag type ( input_fragment_t ), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: fragments (:) logical :: broken integer :: ifrag logical :: in_i , in_j broken = . false . if ( nfrag <= 0 . or . . not . allocated ( fragments )) return do ifrag = 1 , nfrag in_i = any ( fragments ( ifrag )% indices == atom_i ) in_j = any ( fragments ( ifrag )% indices == atom_j ) if ( in_i . neqv . in_j ) then broken = . true . return end if end do end function bond_is_broken","tags":"","url":"proc/bond_is_broken.html"},{"title":"directory_of – metalquicha","text":"private pure function directory_of(path) result(directory) The directory part of a path, or “.” when there is none Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: path Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~directory_of~~CalledByGraph proc~directory_of directory_of proc~read_json_config_file read_json_config_file proc~read_json_config_file->proc~directory_of program~main main program~main->proc~read_json_config_file Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedu