onal_json_impl write_vibrational_json_impl proc~write_json_output->proc~write_vibrational_json_impl Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~session_begin~~CalledByGraph proc~session_begin mqc_session_t%session_begin proc~mqc_session_begin mqc_session_begin proc~mqc_session_begin->proc~session_begin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine session_begin ( this , error ) !! Start MPI. Returns on rank 0; on any other rank, never returns. !! !! A worker spends the rest of the process inside `worker_loop` and exits !! from there. Callers on rank 0 get control back with a live session. class ( mqc_session_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ) :: error if ( this % active ) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"mqc_session: already started\" ) return end if call pic_mpi_init () ! MPI start-up raises IEEE_INVALID and IEEE_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO on every rank ! whenever there is more than one of them -- measured, not guessed: the ! flags are already set on return from pic_mpi_init and are untouched at ! -np 1. They are the MPI implementation's arithmetic, not ours. ! ! Clearing them here rather than before the workers exit is what keeps ! them useful. gfortran reports raised flags at STOP but not at END ! PROGRAM, so the noise surfaced only on the workers, and suppressing it ! at that end would have discarded genuine flags from whatever a worker ! computes. Cleared at the start, a flag set later belongs to us. call ieee_set_flag ( ieee_all , . false .) this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm = comm_world () this % resources % mpi_comms % node_comm = this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm % split () this % rank = this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm % rank () this % n_ranks = this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm % size () this % active = . true . if ( this % rank /= 0 ) call worker_loop ( this ) end subroutine session_begin","tags":"","url":"proc/session_begin.html"},{"title":"session_command – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine session_command(this, command, error) Tell the workers what to do next. Rank 0 only. Type Bound mqc_session_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mqc_session_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: command type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: error Calls proc~~session_command~~CallsGraph proc~session_command mqc_session_t%session_command bcast bcast proc~session_command->bcast proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~session_command->proc~error_set Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~session_command~~CalledByGraph proc~session_command mqc_session_t%session_command proc~session_end mqc_session_t%session_end proc~session_end->proc~session_command proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~session_command proc~mqc_run mqc_run proc~mqc_run->proc~session_run proc~mqc_session_end mqc_session_end proc~mqc_session_end->proc~session_end Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int32), private :: buffer Source Code subroutine session_command ( this , command , error ) !! Tell the workers what to do next. Rank 0 only. class ( mqc_session_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer ( int32 ), intent ( in ) :: command type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ) :: error integer ( int32 ) :: buffer if (. not . this % active ) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"mqc_session: no session to command\" ) return end if if ( this % rank /= 0 ) then ! Only rank 0 ever reaches here in a correct program; a worker issuing ! a command would leave every other rank waiting on a broadcast that ! never comes. call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"mqc_session: only rank 0 may issue commands\" ) return end if buffer = command call bcast ( this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm , buffer , 1_int32 , 0_int32 ) end subroutine session_command","tags":"","url":"proc/session_command.html"},{"title":"session_end – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine session_end(this, error) Release the workers and shut MPI down Type Bound mqc_session_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mqc_session_t ), intent(inout) :: this type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: error Calls proc~~session_end~~CallsGraph proc~session_end mqc_session_t%session_end finalize finalize proc~session_end->finalize pic_mpi_finalize pic_mpi_finalize proc~session_end->pic_mpi_finalize proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~session_end->proc~error_has_error proc~session_command mqc_session_t%session_command proc~session_end->proc~session_command bcast bcast proc~session_command->bcast proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~session_command->proc~error_set Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~session_end~~CalledByGraph proc~session_end mqc_session_t%session_end proc~mqc_session_end mqc_session_end proc~mqc_session_end->proc~session_end Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine session_end ( this , error ) !! Release the workers and shut MPI down class ( mqc_session_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ) :: error if (. not . this % active ) return ! The workers are blocked in a broadcast; this is what wakes them for the ! last time. Skipping it hangs every one of them. if ( this % rank == 0 . and . this % n_ranks > 1 ) then call this % command ( MQC_CMD_STOP , error ) if ( error % has_error ()) return end if call this % resources % mpi_comms % node_comm % finalize () call this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm % finalize () call pic_mpi_finalize () this % active = . false . this % rank = - 1 this % n_ranks = 0 end subroutine session_end","tags":"","url":"proc/session_end.html"},{"title":"session_run – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine session_run(this, settings, sys_geom, terms, n_terms, label, write_output, result, error) Drive a calculation across the job. Rank 0 only. The order here is load-bearing. Everything that can fail on rank 0 –\nparsing the settings, rejecting a bad document – happens before MQC_CMD_RUN goes out. Once that command is sent the workers are\ncommitted to a set of broadcasts, and a rank 0 that discovered a\nproblem afterwards could only return an error to its caller while N-1\nranks sat waiting for a geometry that would never arrive. Type Bound mqc_session_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( mqc_session_t ), intent(inout) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: settings A JSON document of everything but the molecules type( system_geometry_t ), intent(inout) :: sys_geom Read, not modified; intent(inout) because the broadcast it is\npassed to writes on the receiving ranks. integer, intent(in) :: terms (:,:) (n_terms, max_level), 1-based monomer indices, zero-padded integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: n_terms Rows of terms to use; 0 to let the driver generate its own list character(len=*), intent(in) :: label Names the output files. Empty leaves the default. logical, intent(in) :: write_output type( calculation_result_t ), intent(out) :: result type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: error Calls proc~~session_run~~CallsGraph proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~apply_log_level apply_log_level proc~session_run->proc~apply_log_level proc~bcast_string bcast_string proc~session_run->proc~bcast_string proc~bcast_system_geometry bcast_system_geometry proc~session_run->proc~bcast_system_geometry proc~check_supplied_terms check_supplied_terms proc~session_run->proc~check_supplied_terms proc~config_to_driver config_to_driver proc~session_run->proc~config_to_driver proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~session_run->proc~error_has_error proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~session_run->proc~error_set proc~read_json_config_text read_json_config_text proc~session_run->proc~read_json_config_text proc~run_calculation run_calculation proc~session_run->proc~run_calculation proc~session_command mqc_session_t%session_command proc~session_run->proc~session_command proc~set_output_json_filename set_output_json_filename proc~session_run->proc~set_output_json_filename proc~validate_system validate_