tinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~worker_loop~2~~CalledByGraph proc~worker_loop~2 worker_loop proc~session_begin mqc_session_t%session_begin proc~session_begin->proc~worker_loop~2 proc~mqc_session_begin mqc_session_begin proc~mqc_session_begin->proc~session_begin Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int32), private :: command Source Code subroutine worker_loop ( this ) !! Wait for rank 0's instructions until told to stop, then stop !! !! This does not return to its caller. A worker that returned would carry !! on executing the driving script -- the very thing the session exists !! to prevent -- so the process ends here instead. type ( mqc_session_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this integer ( int32 ) :: command do command = MQC_CMD_STOP call bcast ( this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm , command , 1_int32 , 0_int32 ) select case ( command ) case ( MQC_CMD_STOP ) exit case ( MQC_CMD_RUN ) call worker_run ( this ) case default ! An unrecognised command can only mean rank 0 and the workers are ! running different code. Carrying on would deadlock at the next ! collective; stopping at least fails where the cause is. exit end select end do call this % resources % mpi_comms % node_comm % finalize () call this % resources % mpi_comms % world_comm % finalize () call pic_mpi_finalize () stop end subroutine worker_loop","tags":"","url":"proc/worker_loop~2.html"},{"title":"worker_run – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine worker_run(this) A worker’s half of a calculation Receives what rank 0 sends, in the order rank 0 sends it, and then\ncalls the same run_calculation rank 0 does. The two sides are the\nsame three steps written twice rather than shared, because they are\nmirror images and a shared routine would be mostly if (is_root) .\nKeep them in step: a broadcast added to one and not the other hangs\nthe job rather than failing it. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( mqc_session_t ), intent(inout) :: this Calls proc~~worker_run~~CallsGraph proc~worker_run worker_run proc~apply_log_level apply_log_level proc~worker_run->proc~apply_log_level proc~bcast_string bcast_string proc~worker_run->proc~bcast_string proc~bcast_system_geometry bcast_system_geometry proc~worker_run->proc~bcast_system_geometry proc~config_to_driver config_to_driver proc~worker_run->proc~config_to_driver proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~worker_run->proc~error_has_error proc~read_json_config_text read_json_config_text proc~worker_run->proc~read_json_config_text proc~run_calculation run_calculation proc~worker_run->proc~run_calculation configure configure proc~apply_log_level->configure proc~get_logger_level get_logger_level proc~apply_log_level->proc~get_logger_level proc~bcast_integer_array bcast_integer_array proc~bcast_string->proc~bcast_integer_array bcast bcast proc~bcast_system_geometry->bcast proc~bcast_bonds bcast_bonds proc~bcast_system_geometry->proc~bcast_bonds proc~bcast_int_1d bcast_int_1d proc~bcast_system_geometry->proc~bcast_int_1d proc~bcast_int_2d bcast_int_2d proc~bcast_system_geometry->proc~bcast_int_2d proc~bcast_real_2d bcast_real_2d proc~bcast_system_geometry->proc~bcast_real_2d proc~system_destroy system_geometry_t%system_destroy proc~bcast_system_geometry->proc~system_destroy proc~copy_fragment_potentia