elation_keys – metalquicha","text":"private  function correlation_keys() result(keys) Post-Hartree-Fock settings, deliberately not under “scf” The reference and the correlation treatment are configured apart\nbecause they can disagree: a density-fitted Hartree-Fock followed by a\nconventional MP2 is a combination someone will ask for, and one density_fitting shared between them could not express it. The auxiliary basis is deliberately not here. A basis set belongs in model beside the orbital basis it fits, which is where model.aux_basis is, and having two places to name one meant a deck could name both and\nsilently prefer one. Arguments None Return Value type( key_set_t ) Calls proc~~correlation_keys~~CallsGraph proc~correlation_keys correlation_keys proc~allow allow proc~correlation_keys->proc~allow Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~correlation_keys~~CalledByGraph proc~correlation_keys correlation_keys proc~ensure_valid_json ensure_valid_json proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~correlation_keys proc~read_json_config_file read_json_config_file proc~read_json_config_file->proc~ensure_valid_json proc~read_json_config_text read_json_config_text proc~read_json_config_text->proc~ensure_valid_json proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~read_json_config_text proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~read_json_config_text program~main main program~main->proc~read_json_config_file proc~mqc_run mqc_run proc~mqc_run->proc~session_run proc~worker_loop~2 worker_loop proc~worker_loop~2->proc~worker_run proc~session_begin mqc_session_t%session_begin proc~session_begin->proc~worker_loop~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code function correlation_keys () result ( keys ) !! Post-Hartree-Fock settings, deliberately not under \"scf\" !! !! The reference and the correlation treatment are configured apart !! because they can disagree: a density-fitted Hartree-Fock followed by a !! conventional MP2 is a combination someone will ask for, and one !! `density_fitting` shared between them could not express it. !! !! The auxiliary basis is deliberately *not* here. A basis set belongs in !! `model` beside the orbital basis it fits, which is where `model.aux_basis` !! is, and having two places to name one meant a deck could name both and !! silently prefer one. type ( key_set_t ) :: keys call allow ( keys , \"freeze_core\" ) call allow ( keys , \"n_frozen_core\" ) call allow ( keys , \"density_fitting\" ) call allow ( keys , \"scs\" ) call allow ( keys , \"scs_ss\" ) call allow ( keys , \"scs_os\" ) end function correlation_keys","tags":"","url":"proc/correlation_keys.html"},{"title":"dft_keys – metalquicha","text":"private  func