ure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type(json_value), private, pointer :: child logical, private :: found integer, private :: ichild integer, private :: ikey integer, private :: n_children character(len=:), private, allocatable :: name Source Code subroutine check_object ( core , object , path , keys , error ) !! Every key of `object` must be in `keys`, and every required one present type ( json_core ), intent ( inout ) :: core type ( json_value ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: object character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: path !! For the message; \"\" at the root type ( key_set_t ), intent ( in ) :: keys type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ) :: error type ( json_value ), pointer :: child character ( len = :), allocatable :: name integer :: n_children , ichild , ikey logical :: found call core % info ( object , n_children = n_children ) do ichild = 1 , n_children call core % get_child ( object , ichild , child , found ) if (. not . found ) cycle call core % info ( child , name = name ) if (. not . allocated ( name )) cycle if (. not . is_allowed ( keys , name )) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"Unknown key \" // quoted ( path , name ) // & \". Allowed here: \" // allowed_list ( keys )) return end if end do do ikey = 1 , keys % n_required call core % get ( object , trim ( keys % required ( ikey )), child , found ) if (. not . found . or . . not . associated ( child )) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"Missing required key \" // & quoted ( path , trim ( keys % required ( ikey )))) return end if end do end subroutine check_object","tags":"","url":"proc/check_object.html"},{"title":"require – metalquicha","text":"private pure subroutine require(keys, name) Record a key an object must contain Required keys are also allowed ones, so every call here is paired with\nan allow above rather than implying it – the allow-list is what the\nerror message offers the user, and it should read as the whole set. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( key_set_t ), intent(inout) :: keys character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Called by proc~~require~~CalledByGraph proc~require require proc~fragmentation_keys fragmentation_keys proc~fragmentation_keys->proc~require proc~guess_step_keys guess_step_keys proc~guess_step_keys->proc~require proc~model_keys model_keys proc~model_keys->proc~require proc~molecule_keys molecule_keys proc~molecule_keys->proc~require proc~root_keys root_keys proc~root_keys->proc~require proc~schema_keys schema_keys proc~schema_keys->proc~require proc~check_molecules check_molecules proc~check_molecules->proc~molecule_keys proc~ensure_valid_json ensure_valid_json proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~fragmentation_keys proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~model_keys proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~root_keys proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~schema_keys proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~check_molecules proc~validate_guess_group validate_guess_group proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~validate_guess_group proc~validate_guess_group->proc~guess_step_keys proc~read_json_config_file read_json_config_file proc~read_json_config_file->proc~ensure_valid_json proc~read_json_config_text read_json_config_text proc~read_json_config_text->proc~ensure_valid_json proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~read_json_config_text proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~read_json_config_text program~main main program~main->proc~read_json_config_file proc~mqc_run mqc_run proc~mqc_run->proc~session_run proc~worker_loop~2 worker_loop proc~worker_loop~2->proc~worker_run Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine require ( keys , name ) !! Record a key an object must contain !! !! Required keys are also allowed ones, so every call here is paired with !! an `allow` above rather than implying it -- the allow-list is what the !! error message offers the user, and it should read as the whole set. type ( key_set_t ), intent ( inout ) :: keys character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name keys % n_required = keys % n_required + 1 keys % required ( keys % n_required ) = name end subroutine require","tags":"","url":"proc/require.html"},{"title":"validate_guess_group – metalquicha","text":"private  subroutine validate_guess_group(core, root, error) The three rules that make keywords.guess unambiguous keywords.scf.guess and keywords.guess.type must not both be\n     set. The second supersedes the first; refusing both rather than\n     picking one keeps the deck’s meaning independent of reader order. subscf is only meaningful under basis_set_projection . Beside\n     any other guess it would be read, validated and then ignored, which\n     is the failure mode this whole schema exists to prevent. basis_set_projection needs at least one step. A ladder with no\n     rungs is the default guess wearing a longer name. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(json_core), intent(inout) :: core type(json_value), intent(in), pointer :: root type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: error Calls proc~~validate_guess_group~~CallsGraph proc~validate_guess_group validate_guess_group get get proc~validate_guess_group->get get_child get_child proc~validate_guess_group->get_child info info proc~validate_guess_group->info proc~check_object check_object proc~validate_guess_group->proc~check_object proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~validate_guess_group->proc~error_has_error proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~validate_guess_group->proc~error_set proc~guess_step_keys guess_step_keys proc~validate_guess_group->proc~guess_step_keys proc~subscf_keys subscf_keys proc~validate_guess_group->proc~subscf_keys proc~check_object->get proc~check_object->get_child proc~check_object->info proc~check_object->proc~error_set proc~allowed_list allowed_list proc~check_object->proc~allowed_list proc~is_allowed is_allowed proc~check_object->proc~is_allowed proc~quoted quoted proc~check_object->proc~quoted proc~allow allow proc~guess_step_keys->proc~allow proc~require require proc~guess_step_keys->proc~require proc~subscf_keys->proc~allow Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~validate_guess_group~~CalledByGraph proc~validate_guess_group validate_guess_group proc~ensure_valid_json ensure_valid_json proc~ensure_valid_json->proc~validate_guess_group proc~read_json_config_file read_json_config_file proc~read_json_config_file->proc~ensure_valid_json proc~read_json_config_text read_json_config_text proc~read_json_config_text->proc~ensure_valid_json proc~session_run mqc_session_t%session_run proc~session_run->proc~read_json_config_text proc~worker_run worker_run proc~worker_run->proc~read_json_config_text program~main main program~main->proc~read_json_config_file proc~mqc_run mqc_run proc~mqc_run->proc~session_run proc~worker_loop~2 worker_loop proc~worker_loop~2->proc~worker_run proc~session_begin mqc_session_t%session_begin proc~session_begin->proc~worker_loop~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private :: found character(len=:), private, allocatable :: gtype type(json_value), private, pointer :: guess logical, private :: has_scf_guess integer, private :: i logical, private :: is_projection type(json_value), private, pointer :: keywords integer, private :: n_steps type(json_value), private, pointer :: scf type(json_value), private, pointer :: step type(json_value), private, pointer :: steps type(json_value), private, pointer :: subscf Source Code subroutine validate_guess_group ( core , root , error ) !! The three rules that make `keywords.guess` unambiguous !! !!   1. `keywords.scf.guess` and `keywords.guess.type` must not both be !!      set. The second supersedes the first; refusing both rather than !!      picking one keeps the deck's meaning independent of reader order. !!   2. `subscf` is only meaningful under `basis_set_projection`. Beside !!      any other guess it would be read, validated and then ignored, which !!      is the failure mode this whole schema exists to prevent. !!   3. `basis_set_projection` needs at least one step. A ladder with no !!      rungs is the default guess wearing a longer name. type ( json_core ), intent ( inout ) :: core type ( json_value ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: root type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ) :: error type ( json_value ), pointer :: keywords , guess , scf , subscf , steps , step character ( len = :), allocatable :: gtype logical :: found , has_scf_guess , is_projection integer :: n_steps , i call core % get ( root , \"keywords\" , keywords , found ) if (. not . found . or . . not . associated ( keywords )) return call core % get ( keywords , \"guess\" , guess , found ) if (. not . found . or . . not . associated ( guess )) return has_scf_guess = . false . call core % get ( keywords , \"scf\" , scf , found ) if ( found . and . associated ( scf )) then call core % get ( scf , \"guess\" , steps , has_scf_guess ) end if call core % get ( guess , \"type\" , steps , found ) if ( found . and . associated ( steps )) then call core % get ( guess , \"type\" , gtype ) end if if ( has_scf_guess . and . allocated ( gtype )) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"keywords.scf.guess and keywords.guess.type \" // & \"both set the initial guess. Use keywords.guess.type; \" // & \"keywords.scf.guess is the older spelling and is superseded.\" ) return end if is_projection = . false . if ( allocated ( gtype )) is_projection = trim ( adjustl ( gtype )) == \"basis_set_projection\" call core % get ( guess , \"subscf\" , subscf , found ) if ( found . and . associated ( subscf )) then if (. not . is_projection ) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"keywords.guess.subscf only means something \" // & \"for type 'basis_set_projection'; beside any other guess it \" // & \"would be read and then ignored\" ) return end if call check_object ( core , subscf , \"keywords.guess.subscf\" , subscf_keys (), error ) if ( error % has_error ()) return call core % get ( subscf , \"steps\" , steps , found ) if ( found . and . associated ( steps )) then call core % info ( steps , n_children = n_steps ) do i = 1 , n_steps call core % get_child ( steps , i , step , found ) if (. not . found . or . . not . associated ( step )) cycle call check_object ( core , step , \"keywords.guess.subscf.steps\" , & guess_step_keys (), error ) if ( error % has_error ()) return end do end if end if if ( is_projection ) then n_steps = 0 call core % get ( guess , \"subscf.steps\" , steps , found ) if ( found . and . associated ( steps )) call core % info ( steps , n_children = n_steps ) if ( n_steps < 1 ) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"guess type 'basis_set_projection' needs \" // & \"keywords.guess.subscf.steps with at least one basis to \" // & \"converge before the target one\" ) return end if end if end subroutine validate_guess_group","tags":"","url":"proc/validate_guess_group.html"},{"title":"write_json_output – metalquicha","text":"public  subroutine write_json_output(output_data) THE single entry point for all JSON output Dispatches to the appropriate JSON writer based on output_mode.\nThis is the ONLY place in the codebase where JSON files are written. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( json_output_data_t ), intent(in) :: output_data Calls proc~~write_json_output~~CallsGraph proc~write_json_output write_json_output error error proc~write_json_output->error proc~write_fragment_table write_fragment_table proc~write_json_output->proc~write_fragment_table proc~write_gmbe_pie_json_impl write_gmbe_pie_json