al ( dp ), intent ( in ) :: tolerance logical :: is_bonded real ( dp ) :: r_i , r_j , distance is_bonded = . false . r_i = element_covalent_radius ( sys_geom % element_numbers ( iatom )) r_j = element_covalent_radius ( sys_geom % element_numbers ( jatom )) ! No radius, no opinion. if ( r_i <= 0.0_dp . or . r_j <= 0.0_dp ) return distance = to_angstrom ( norm2 ( sys_geom % coordinates (:, iatom ) - & sys_geom % coordinates (:, jatom ))) is_bonded = ( distance < tolerance * ( r_i + r_j )) end function bonded","tags":"","url":"proc/bonded.html"},{"title":"find_root – metalquicha","text":"private pure recursive function find_root(component, node) result(root) Representative of a node’s component Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: component (:) integer, intent(in) :: node Return Value integer Called by proc~~find_root~~CalledByGraph proc~find_root find_root proc~find_root->proc~find_root proc~connected_components connected_components proc~connected_components->proc~find_root proc~auto_monomers auto_monomers proc~auto_monomers->proc~connected_components proc~build_residues build_residues proc~build_residues->proc~connected_components proc~mqc_system_auto_monomers mqc_system_auto_monomers proc~mqc_system_auto_monomers->proc~auto_monomers proc~run_geometry_optimization run_geometry_optimization proc~run_geometry_optimization->proc~build_residues program~main main program~main->proc~run_geometry_optimization Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface