ity-fitted engine and the exchange-correlation energy and\npotential from its grid engine; the SCF itself runs in mqc_cuest_scf . Density fitting is not optional here. cuEST has no conventional\nfour-index ERI path, so J (and K for hybrids) are always fitted and an\nauxiliary JKFIT basis is required. use_density_fitting is therefore\nignored by this backend rather than switchable. The amount of exact exchange is never assumed from the functional name:\nit is queried from cuEST’s XC plan and handed to the DF plan, so a hybrid\ncannot end up with mismatched Coulomb and XC definitions. Uses mqc_method_config mqc_error mqc_cuest_iface pic_types mqc_physical_fragment mqc_semi_numerical_hessian mqc_cuest_bridge mqc_config_types mqc_result_types mqc_libcint_bridge mqc_method_base module~~mqc_method_dft~~UsesGraph module~mqc_method_dft mqc_method_dft module~mqc_config_types mqc_config_types module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_config_types module~mqc_cuest_bridge mqc_cuest_bridge module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_cuest_bridge module~mqc_cuest_iface mqc_cuest_iface module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_cuest_iface module~mqc_error mqc_error module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_error module~mqc_libcint_bridge mqc_libcint_bridge module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_libcint_bridge module~mqc_method_base mqc_method_base module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_method_base module~mqc_method_config mqc_method_config module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_method_config module~mqc_physical_fragment mqc_physical_fragment module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_physical_fragment module~mqc_result_types mqc_result_types module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_result_types module~mqc_semi_numerical_hessian mqc_semi_numerical_hessian module~mqc_method_dft->module~mqc_semi_numerical_hessian pic_types pic_types module~mqc_method_dft->pic_types module~mqc_config_types->module~mqc_physical_fragment module~mqc_config_types->pic_types module~mqc_calc_types mqc_calc_types module~mqc_config_types->module~mqc_calc_types module~mqc_c