c, allocatable :: elements (:) integer, public :: natoms = 0 Defaulted because a config in multi-molecule mode leaves its\ntop-level geometry untouched, and an undefined atom count there is\na trap for any consumer that reads it before checking nmol. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: destroy => geometry_destroy Subroutines private  subroutine geometry_destroy (this) Clean up allocated memory in geometry_type Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( geometry_type ), intent(inout) :: this","tags":"","url":"module/mqc_geometry.html"},{"title":"mqc_diis – metalquicha","text":"Holds the DIIS history and produces the extrapolated Fock matrix. Split out of the cuEST SCF driver for two reasons. It is pure linear\nalgebra over flat vectors with no integrals backend behind it, so it builds\nand is unit-tested without a GPU – which the SCF driver is not, since that\nneeds libcuest and an sm_80 card. And it gives the device port a host\nreference to diff against: the failure mode of a device DIIS is a silently\nstale history producing plausible-but-wrong coefficients, which only shows\nup against a known-good implementation. Vectors are stored flat, one column per subspace entry, which serves the\nrestricted case (one n_ao*n_ao Fock) and the unrestricted case (both spins\nstacked into one vector) through the same code, and is the layout a device\nreduction wants: contiguous and coalesced.\nRing slot holding the age-th oldest entry\nExtrapolation weights from a cached overlap matrix Uses pic_types module~~mqc_diis~~UsesGraph module~mqc_diis mqc_diis pic_types pic_types module~mqc_diis->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=dp), private, parameter :: PIVOT_FLOOR = 1.0e-14_dp The two procedures above are the parts of DIIS that have nothing to do\nBelow this a pivot is treated as singular and extrapolation is skipped Derived Types type, public :: diis_state_t One SCF’s worth of DIIS history Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=dp), public, allocatable :: error_history (:,:) (n_error, max_vectors) real(kind=dp), public, allocatable :: fock_history (:,:) (n_fock, max_vectors) integer, public :: max_vectors = 0 Subspace size integer, public :: n_error = 0 Elements in one error vector integer, public :: n_fock = 0 Elements in one Fock vector integer, public :: n_stored = 0 Entries currently held (<= max_vectors) integer, public :: newest = 0 Slot holding the most recent entry real(kind=dp), public, allocatable :: overlap (:,:) (max_vectors, max_vectors) cached in slot coordinates.\nKept across iterations: pushing one vector changes exactly one row\nand column, so rebuilding the whole matrix each iteration costs\nO(n_stored&#94;2 * n_error) where O(n_stored * n_error) suffices. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: count => diis_count procedure, public :: destroy => diis_destroy procedure, public :: extrapolate => diis_extrapolate procedure, public :: init => diis_init procedure, public :: push => diis_push Functions public pure function diis_slot_of_age (newest, n_stored, max_vectors, age) result(slot) Slot holding the age-th oldest entry, age = 1 .. n_stored Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: newest integer, intent(in) :: n_stored integer, intent(in) :: max_vectors integer, intent(in) :: age Return Value integer private pure function diis_count (this) result(n) Number of entries currently in the subspace Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( diis_state_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer private pure function slot_of_age (this, age) result(slot) diis_slot_of_age for this state’s ring Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( diis_state_t ), intent(in) :: this integer, intent(in) :: age Return Value integer Subroutines public  subroutine diis_coefficients (overlap, newest, n_stored, max_vectors, coefficients, ok) Extrapolation weights, oldest-first, from a cached error overlap matrix Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: overlap (:,:) (max_vectors, max_vectors), slot coordinates integer, intent(in) :: newest integer, intent(in) :: n_stored integer, intent(in) :: max_vectors real(kind=dp), intent(out), allocatable :: coefficients (:) (n_stored+1), oldest first. The trailing entry is the Lagrange\nmultiplier enforcing sum(c) = 1 and is not a weight – read\n1..n_stored only. logical, intent(out) :: ok False when the subspace is too small or singular private  subroutine diis_destroy (this) Release the history Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( diis_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine diis_extrapolate (this, fock, ok) Replace fock with the DIIS combination of the stored Fock matrices Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( diis_state_t ), intent(in) :: this real(kind=dp), intent(inout) :: fock (this%n_fock) logical, intent(out) :: ok private  subroutine diis_init (this, max_vectors, n_fock, n_error) Allocate the history for a subspace of max_vectors entries Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( diis_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer, intent(in) :: max_vectors Subspace size integer, intent(in) :: n_fock Elements in one Fock vector integer, intent(in) :: n_error Elements in one error vector private  subroutine diis_push (this, fock, error_vector) Add one (Fock, error) pair, evicting the oldest entry when full Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( diis_state_t ), intent(inout) :: this real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: fock (this%n_fock) real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: error_vector (this%n_error) private  subroutine solve_diis (b_matrix, coefficients, ok) Solve the small DIIS linear system by Gaussian elimination Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: b_matrix (:,:) real(kind=dp), intent(out), allocatable :: coefficients (:) logical, intent(out) :: ok","tags":"","url":"module/mqc_diis.html"},{"title":"mqc_physical_fragment – metalquicha","text":"Physical molecular fragment representation and geometry handling Provides data structures and utilities for managing molecular fragments\nwith atomic coordinates, electronic properties, and geometric operations.\nBond connectivity type\nSingle molecular fragment type\nComplete system geometry type\nSystem geometry initialization\nExtract fragment from system\nCharge/multiplicity a set of monomers forms\nBuild fragment from explicit atom indices (for intersections)\nValidate fragment has no overlapping atoms Redistribute hydrogen cap gradients to original atoms\nRedistribute hydrogen cap Hessian to original atoms\nRedistribute hydrogen cap dipole derivatives to original atoms\nUnit conversion utilities\nCalculate minimal distance between monomers in a fragment Uses mqc_error pic_types mqc_physical_constants mqc_elements mqc_cgto mqc_xyz_reader mqc_geometry module~~mqc_physical_fragment~~UsesGraph module~mqc_physical_fragment mqc_physical_fragment module~mqc_cgto mqc_cgto module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_cgto module~mqc_elements mqc_elements module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_elements module~mqc_error mqc_error module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_error module~mqc_geometry mqc_geometry module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_geometry module~mqc_physical_constants mqc_physical_constants module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_physical_constants module~mqc_xyz_reader mqc_xyz_reader module~mqc_