rbit parameters, orders 6 to 5810 Each record is one orbit of the octahedral group: a code saying which\norbit type, the seed parameters a and b, and the weight carried by every\npoint in it. mqc_lebedev expands them into points. Records for order\nLEBEDEV_ORDERS(i) run from ORDER_OFFSET(i) to ORDER_OFFSET(i+1)-1. These are the published Lebedev-Laikov parameters [V.I. Lebedev and\nD.N. Laikov, Dokl. Math. 59, 477 (1999)] and integrate polynomials up to\ndegree 131 to a relative accuracy of 2e-14. The weights of each grid sum\nto 1, so the surface of the unit sphere is normalised out. Generated by scratchpad/gen_lebedev_fortran.py – do not edit by hand. Uses pic_types module~~mqc_lebedev_data~~UsesGraph module~mqc_lebedev_data mqc_lebedev_data pic_types pic_types module~mqc_lebedev_data->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~mqc_lebedev_data~~UsedByGraph module~mqc_lebedev_data mqc_lebedev_data module~mqc_lebedev mqc_lebedev module~mqc_lebedev->module~mqc_lebedev_data module~mqc_dft_grid mqc_dft_grid module~mqc_dft_grid->module~mqc_lebedev Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguis