ariables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: OPT_ALGO_CG = 2 Conjugate gradient integer, public, parameter :: OPT_ALGO_LBFGS = 3 Limited-memory BFGS integer, public, parameter :: OPT_ALGO_PRFO = 4 Partitioned rational function, for a saddle integer, public, parameter :: OPT_ALGO_SD = 1 Steepest descent integer, public, parameter :: OPT_ALGO_UNKNOWN = 0 integer, public, parameter :: OPT_COORDS_CARTESIAN = 1 integer, public, parameter :: OPT_COORDS_DLC = 3 Delocalised internal coordinates integer, public, parameter :: OPT_COORDS_DLC_TC = 5 DLC over a total connection scheme One residue, totally connected. Unlike plain dlc this does not fail on\na cluster – the total connection supplies the coordinates spanning the\nmolecules that no bond provides – but it pays that quadratic cost over\nthe whole system rather than within a residue. integer, public, parameter :: OPT_COORDS_HDLC = 2 Hybrid delocalised internal coordinates integer, public, parameter :: OPT_COORDS_HDLC_TC = 4 HDLC over a total connection scheme The primitive internals of a residue are built from every atom pair in\nit rather than from the perceived bonds. That is what makes it useful on\na system whose connectivity is not what a covalent-radius rule says: a\nweakly bound complex the perception splits, an ion pair it merges, a\ntransition state where a bond is half formed. The cost is quadratic in\nresidue size where a bond list is linear, so it is for small residues. integer, public, parameter :: OPT_COORDS_UNKNOWN = 0 Abstract Interfaces abstract interface public  subroutine energy_gradient_i(n_atoms, coords, energy, gradient, status) Energy and gradient at a geometry, in atomic units Coordinates are Bohr and the gradient is Hartree/Bohr, both in the\nsystem’s own atom order. Fragmentation and hydrogen caps have\nalready been folded back in by the time an engine sees this, so an\nengine never learns whether the number it was handed came from one\ncalculation or from twenty thousand. status is 0 for success. An engine must stop on anything else\nrather than step on a gradient that was never computed – a failed\nfragment leaves the array at whatever it held, which reads as a\nperfectly plausible small gradient. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: n_atoms real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: coords (3,n_atoms) real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: energy real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: gradient (3,n_atoms) integer, intent(out) :: status abstract interface public  subroutine step_callback_i(n_atoms, coords, energy) One accepted geometry, as the optimization passes through it Called by the engine for each step it accepts – not for every\nenergy evaluation, which includes the trial points of a line\nsearch and would make a trajectory that goes backwards. What the\ndriver does with it (writes a frame, records it for the output\ndocument) is not the engine’s business. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: n_atoms real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: coords (3,n_atoms) real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: energy Derived Types type, public :: optimizer_settings_t One optimization’s settings, as the deck asked for them Read more… Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public :: algorithm = OPT_ALGO_LBFGS integer, public :: coordinates = OPT_COORDS_CARTESIAN real(kind=dp), public :: energy_tolerance = DEFAULT_OPT_ENERGY_TOLERANCE Convergence on the energy change, Hartree. Negative: engine default logical, public :: freeze_terms = .true. Choose the MBE term list once, at the starting geometry, and keep\nit for every step. See mqc_geometry_optimizer for why an\noptimization on a re-screened list is optimizing a moving target. real(kind=dp), public :: gradient_tolerance = DEFAULT_OPT_GRADIENT_TOLERANCE Convergence on the largest gradient component, Hartree/Bohr integer, public :: lbfgs_memory = DEFAULT_OPT_LBFGS_MEMORY Steps of curvature history. Negative: engine default real(kind=dp), public :: max_step = DEFAULT_OPT_MAX_STEP Longest step the engine may take, Bohr. Negative: engine default integer, public :: max_steps = DEFAULT_OPT_MAX_STEPS Give up after this many steps without converging integer, public :: print_level = DEFAULT_OPT_PRINT_LEVEL How much the engine itself prints. Negative: engine default logical, public :: trajectory = .true. Record every accepted geometry, for analysing the path afterwards.\nWorth turning off for a large system optimized over many steps:\nthe geometries are held until the run ends so they can be written\nas one document, which is 3N doubles per step of memory. Functions public pure function algorithm_from_string (text) result(algorithm) Parse the stepping algorithm a deck asked for Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text Return Value integer public pure function algorithm_to_string (algorithm) result(text) Name a stepping algorithm, for the log and the output document Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: algorithm Return Value character(len=:), allocatable public pure function coordinates_from_string (text) result(coordinates) Parse the coordinate system a deck asked for Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text Return Value integer public pure function coordinates_to_string (coordinates) result(text) Name a coordinate system, for the log and the output document Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: coordinates Return Value character(len=:), allocatable private pure function lowercase (text) result(lowered) Case-insensitive comparison, the way mqc_calc_types does it Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text Return Value character(len=len_trim)","tags":"","url":"module/mqc_optimizer_types.html"},{"title":"mqc_mpi_comms – metalquicha","text":"Container type for MPI communicators - extensible for future parallelism pattern