 be honoured is refused rather than quietly substituted – which\nis the whole reason for naming one. A deck that says cuest and silently\ngot the CPU path would report timings and a provenance that were not true. integer, public, parameter :: BACKEND_CUEST = 1 integer, public, parameter :: BACKEND_LIBCINT = 2 Derived Types type, public :: cuest_scf_settings_t Method-independent description of one cuEST SCF calculation Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: allow_crap_scf = .false. Keep a non-converged SCF instead of failing the fragment. Same\nmeaning and same default as the xTB path – one physical condition\nmust not have two behaviours depending on which backend ran it. integer, public :: angular_points = 302 XC grid Lebedev order character(len=32), public :: aux_basis_set = \"def2-universal-jkfit\" integer, public :: backend = BACKEND_AUTO One of BACKEND_*. Resolved from the deck’s backend key. character(len=32), public :: basis_set = \"sto-3g\" Orbital basis set name integer, public :: cc_diis_size = 8 integer, public :: cc_max_iter = 100 real(kind=dp), public :: cc_tolerance = 1.0e-8_dp logical, public :: cc_triples = .false. Run the perturbative (T) after CCSD logical, public :: corr_density_fitting = .false. RI for the correlation step logical, public :: density_fitting = .false. real(kind=dp), public :: density_tol = 1.0e-6_dp integer, public :: device_rank = 0 Node-local MPI rank; decides which GPU this rank binds to integer, public :: diis_size = 8 real(kind=dp), public :: energy_tol = 1.0e-8_dp logical, public :: freeze_core = .false. character(len=32), public :: functional = \"\" Exchange-correlation functional; empty means Hartree-Fock integer, public :: grid_level = 3 character(len=32), public :: guess = \"auto\" Initial guess: ‘core’, ‘gwh’, ‘sac’, ‘sad’, ‘basis_set_projection’,\nor ‘auto’ type( guess_step_t ), public, allocatable :: guess_steps (:) The basis ladder for ‘basis_set_projection’, one entry per\npreliminary SCF in order. The target basis is basis_set and is not\nrepeated, so STO-3G then 6-31G then cc-pVTZ is two steps. Read more… integer, public :: max_iter = 100 integer, public :: n_frozen_core = -1 -1 means count it from the elements type( pcm_config_t ), public :: pcm Read by the CPU backend only; cuEST always fits.\nAuxiliary (JKFIT) basis. Required: cuEST fits J and K always. integer, public :: radial_points = 75 XC grid radial points per atom logical, public :: run_cc = .false. logical, public :: run_mp2 = .false. real(kind=dp), public :: scs_os = 1.0_dp real(kind=dp), public :: scs_ss = 1.0_dp Spin-component scaling, one for plain MP2 logical, public :: spherical = .true. Pure (spherical) vs Cartesian angular functions logical, public :: unrestricted = .false. Force UHF/UKS even for a closed shell logical, public :: use_diis = .true. logical, public :: verbose = .false. Print the SCF iteration table Subroutines public  subroutine parse_backend_name (name, kind, error) A deck’s backend name to one of BACKEND_* Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name integer, intent(out) :: kind type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: error","tags":"","url":"module/mqc_cuest_iface.html"},{"title":"mqc_program_limits – metalquicha","text":"Contains compile-time limits and default values for the metalquicha program.\nThese are tunable parameter that control memory allocation and algorithm behavior. Uses pic_types module~~mqc_program_limits~~UsesGraph module~mqc_program_limits mqc_program_limits pic_types pic_types module~mqc_program_limits->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges co