ray (:,:) integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: count integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: max_len private recursive subroutine combine_util (arr, n, r, index, data, i, out_array, count) Utility for generating combinations recursively\nUses int64 for count to handle large numbers of combinations that overflow int32. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: arr (:) integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: r integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: index integer(kind=default_int), intent(inout) :: data (:) integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: i integer(kind=default_int), intent(inout) :: out_array (:,:) integer(kind=int64), intent(inout) :: count","tags":"","url":"module/mqc_combinatorics.html"},{"title":"mqc_capi_system – metalquicha","text":"The molecule, its monomer partition and its bonds, reachable from C. Wraps system_geometry_t , which already carries all three – the atoms,\nthe partition fragments are built from, and the connectivity hydrogen\ncapping needs. Nothing new is modelled here; this is the way in. Three conventions that are invisible in the signatures and wrong by\ndefault if a caller assumes otherwise: Coordinates arrive in Angstrom and are stored in Bohr. Everything\n    inside metalquicha is atomic units; every input path converts. A\n    caller passing Bohr gets a molecule 1.89 times too large, which\n    converges to a perfectly plausible wrong energy. Atom indices are 0-based , in the monomer partition and in the\n    bonds alike, matching the JSON schema and bond_t . Monomer indices\n    in a fragment term list are 1-based – different things, counted\n    differently, and the one trap in this interface. Bonds must be declared, and broken ones must be declared broken. set_bonds is not optional: a system that never calls it is refused\n    rather than assumed to have none, because those two states are\n    indistinguishable from outside and only one of them is safe. Passing n_bonds = 0 is the way to say a system has nothing to cut. Where the connectivity is given, every bond crossing a monomer\nboundary must carry is_broken . That is checked here rather than\ntrusted, because the alternative is a fragment with a dangling\nvalence: an uncapped radical treated as a closed shell, which\nconverges to a plausible number and warns about nothing.\nExposed for the sibling C-API modules that must open a system handle,\nnot for general use. Nothing outside src/interface should hold one:\nthe rest of the code works in system_geometry_t . Uses mqc_error pic_types mqc_physical_fragment mqc_bond_perception iso_c_binding module~~mqc_capi_system~~UsesGraph module~mqc_capi_system mqc_capi_system iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~mqc_capi_system->iso_c_binding module~mqc_bond_perception mqc_bond_perception module~mqc_capi_system->module~mqc_bond_perception module~mqc_error mqc_error module~mqc_capi_system->module~mqc_error module~mqc_physical_fragment mqc_physical_fragment module~mqc_capi_system->module~mqc_physical_fragment pic_types pic_types module~mqc_capi_system->pic_types module~mqc_bond_perception->module~mqc_error module~mqc_bond_perception->module~mqc_physical_fragment module~mqc_bond_perception->pic_types module~mqc_elements mqc_elements module~mqc_bond_perception->module~mqc_elements module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_error module~mqc_physical_fragment->pic_types module~mqc_cgto mqc_cgto module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_cgto module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_elements module~mqc_geometry mqc_geometry module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_geometry module~mqc_physical_constants mqc_physical_constants module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_physical_constants module~mqc_xyz_reader mqc_xyz_reader module~mqc_physical_fragment->module~mqc_xyz_reader module~mqc_cgto->pic_types module~mqc_elements->pic_types pic_ascii pic_ascii module~mqc_elements->pic_ascii module~mqc_geometry->pic_types module~mqc_physical_constants->pic_types module~mqc_xyz_reader->module~mqc_error module~mqc_xyz_reader->pic_types module~mqc_xyz_reader->module~mqc_geometry Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~mqc_capi_system~~UsedByGraph module~mqc_capi_system mqc_capi_system module~mqc_capi_run mqc_capi_run module~mqc_capi_run->module~mqc_capi_system Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private, parameter :: MESSAGE_LEN = 512 integer(kind=c_int), private, parameter :: MQC_BAD_HANDLE = 2 integer(kind=c_int), private, parameter :: MQC_FAIL = 1 integer(kind=c_int), private, parameter :: MQC_OK = 0 character(len=MESSAGE_LEN), private, save :: last_message = \"\" Derived Types type, public :: system_handle_t The system, plus what the caller has actually told us about it Read more… Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, public :: bonds_declared = .false. type( system_geometry_t ), public :: geom Functions public  function mqc_system_auto_monomers (handle, tolerance) result(status) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_auto_monomers\") Make each covalently connected molecule a monomer Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle real(kind=c_double), value :: tolerance Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_bonds_declared (handle) result(declared) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_bonds_declared\") Whether the caller has said anything about bonds at all Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_count_missing_bonds (handle, tolerance) result(n_missing) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_count_missing_bonds\") How many cuts the geometry implies that the declared bonds omit Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle real(kind=c_double), value :: tolerance Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_n_atoms (handle) result(n) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_n_atoms\") Atoms in the system, or -1 for a bad handle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_n_bonds (handle) result(n) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_n_bonds\") Bonds recorded, or -1 for a bad handle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_n_monomers (handle) result(n) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_n_monomers\") Monomers in the partition, or -1 for a bad handle Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_new () result(handle) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_new\") Allocate an empty system and return its handle Arguments None Return Value type(c_ptr) public  function mqc_system_perceive_bonds (handle, tolerance) result(status) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_perceive_bonds\") Work the connectivity out from the geometry and declare it Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle real(kind=c_double), value :: tolerance Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_set_bonds (handle, n_bonds, atom_i, atom_j, order, is_broken) result(status) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_set_bonds\") The connectivity hydrogen capping works from Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle integer(kind=c_int), value :: n_bonds integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: atom_i (n_bonds) 0-based integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: atom_j (n_bonds) 0-based integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: order (n_bonds) integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: is_broken (n_bonds) non-zero = broken Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_set_geometry (handle, n_atoms, atomic_numbers, coordinates, charge, multiplicity) result(status) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_set_geometry\") The atoms, in Angstrom Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle integer(kind=c_int), value :: n_atoms integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: atomic_numbers (n_atoms) real(kind=c_double), intent(in) :: coordinates (3*n_atoms) x,y,z per atom, contiguous, ANGSTROM integer(kind=c_int), value :: charge integer(kind=c_int), value :: multiplicity Return Value integer(kind=c_int) public  function mqc_system_set_monomers (handle, n_monomers, max_size, sizes, atoms, charges, multiplicities) result(status) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_set_monomers\") The partition fragments are built from Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle integer(kind=c_int), value :: n_monomers integer(kind=c_int), value :: max_size integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: sizes (n_monomers) integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: atoms (max_size*n_monomers) 0-based atom indices, column per monomer, unused slots ignored integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: charges (n_monomers) integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: multiplicities (n_monomers) Return Value integer(kind=c_int) private pure function int_text (value) result(text) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: value Return Value character(len=:), allocatable private pure function monomer_of (sys, atom) result(imon) Which monomer holds a 0-based atom, or 0 if the partition omits it Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( system_geometry_t ), intent(in) :: sys integer(kind=c_int), intent(in) :: atom Return Value integer Subroutines public  subroutine mqc_system_free (handle) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_free\") Release a system. Safe on a null handle. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: handle public  subroutine mqc_system_last_error (buffer_len, buffer) bind(C, name=\"mqc_system_last_error\") Copy the most recent failure message out as a C string Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), value :: buffer_len character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(inout) :: buffer (buffer_len) private  subroutine release (sys) Free everything the system owns Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( system_geometry_t ), intent(inout) :: sys","tags":"","url":"module/mqc_capi_system.html"},{"title":"mqc_bcast – metalquicha","text":"Integer arrays and character strings, from rank 0 to everyone. pic-mpi’s bcast covers scalars and real arrays; integer arrays and\nstrings it only moves point to point. Those are exactly the shapes an\nexternally driven run needs to send its workers – atomic numbers,\nmonomer partitions, bond lists, term lists, and the config as text – so\nthey are built here from send / recv rather than left to each caller to\nopen-code. Linear, not a tree. Rank 0 sends to every other rank in turn, which\nis O(P) messages where a tree would be O(log P). That is deliberate for\nnow: this runs once per calculation, during setup, against fragment\nevaluation that takes minutes to hours. It is the wrong shape if it ever\nmoves inside a loop, and the place to fix it is here rather than at every\ncall site. Every routine is collective: all ranks call it, rank 0 supplies the data\nand the others receive it. A rank that skips one leaves the others\nwaiting on a message that never comes, which is a hang rather than an\nerror – so these are called from paths where every rank arrives, not\nfrom inside a rank-guarded branch.\nAllocatable integer array to every rank\nAllocatable double array to every rank\nDeferred-length character to every rank Uses mqc_mpi_tags pic_types pic_mpi_lib module~~mqc_bcast~~UsesGraph module~mqc_bcast mqc_bcast module~mqc_mpi_tags mqc_mpi_tags module~mqc_bcast->module~mqc_mpi_tags pic_mpi_lib pic_mpi_lib module~mqc_bcast->pic_mpi_lib pic_types pic_types module~mqc_bcast->pic_types module~mqc_mpi_tags->pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~mqc_bcast~~UsedByGraph module~mqc_bcast mqc_bcast module~mqc_bcast_system mqc_bcast_system module~mqc_bcast_system->module~mqc_bcast module~mqc_session mqc_session module~mqc_session->module~mqc_bcast module~mqc_session->module~mqc_bcast_system module~mqc_capi_run mqc_capi_run module~mqc_capi_run->module~mqc_session module~mqc_capi_session mqc_capi_session module~mqc_capi_run->module~mqc_capi_session module~mqc_capi_session->module~mqc_session Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\